From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 07:56:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] 3221 winhttp: options, proxy, decompression, bounds, times
 and statistics, IWinHttpRequest options and stream

The option handlers of sessions, connections and requests were FIXME stubs for
most options. Now (from the "Option flags" table of the WinHTTP documentation):
- stored options of the session handed down to its requests (CONNECT_RETRIES,
  MAX_HTTP_AUTOMATIC_REDIRECTS, MAX_HTTP_STATUS_CONTINUE, MAX_RESPONSE_HEADER_SIZE,
  MAX_RESPONSE_DRAIN_SIZE, MAX_CONNS_PER_SERVER / _1_0_SERVER, CODEPAGE,
  ENCODE_EXTRA, DECOMPRESSION, ENABLE_HTTP_PROTOCOL, ... ), HANDLE_TYPE, CALLBACK,
  PARENT_HANDLE, SECURE_PROTOCOLS (the policy default), USER_AGENT, EXTENDED_ERROR,
  HTTP_PROTOCOL_USED, and the NULL-handle options (PROXY, HTTP_VERSION,
  ENABLETRACING, WORKER_THREAD_COUNT once, GLOBAL_PROXY/SERVER_CREDS behind the
  ShareCredsWithWinHttp policy);
- WINHTTP_OPTION_PROXY on sessions and requests (the request's proxy re-points
  its connection), IS_PROXY_CONNECT_RESPONSE / RECEIVE_PROXY_CONNECT_RESPONSE;
- behaviours: 1xx answers skipped up to MAX_HTTP_STATUS_CONTINUE, header block
  bound (ERROR_WINHTTP_HEADER_SIZE_OVERFLOW), drain bound, EXPIRE_CONNECTION,
  per-server connection limit that makes requests wait, CONNECT_RETRIES and
  IPV6_FAST_FALLBACK trying the other addresses of a host, gzip/deflate
  decompression (Accept-Encoding set, inflated reads and data-available counts),
  URL code page, REQUEST_TIMES and REQUEST_STATS, SERVER_CERT_CHAIN_CONTEXT,
  server/proxy SPN, shared credentials;
- WinHttpQueryHeaders: the table was misaligned past 70 and lacked the legacy
  names (Content-Description, Link, Forwarded, From, Refresh, Content-Disposition,
  Proxy-Support, Authentication-Info);
- websocket CLOSE_TIMEOUT; IWinHttpRequest::Option for all documented options,
  SetClientCertificate / SelectCertificate ("location\store\subject"), and the
  response stream (read-only, CopyTo, Stat, Clone, lock errors).
Also: a request closes its connection when it goes away; todo_wine of Invoke removed.

